(defrule runtime -> runtime-harness runtime-cycle runtime-boundaries runtime-subsystems subsystem-list runtime-modes runtime-routing runtime-delegated-planning runtime-planner-stages runtime-plan-review runtime-normal-mode runtime-replanning runtime-plan-design-rationale changes)
(defrule runtime-harness -> :instruction "実行時の動作を統べる仕組みと、それがモデルをどう変えるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "The runtime behavior is governed by the agent harness, the orchestration infrastructure introduced in Section 2.2 that turns a stateless LLM into a persistent, tool-using, self-correcting agent.")
(defrule runtime-cycle -> :instruction "中心のループが 1 回の繰り返しで行う段階を挙げて 1 文で書く" :sample "The ReAct loop at the center of Figure 4 executes six phases per iteration: pre-check and compaction, thinking, self-critique, action, tool execution, and post-processing.")
(defrule runtime-boundaries -> :instruction "入力を受ける部分と、実行中にも届くメッセージの扱いを 1 文で書く。出力側の後処理があれば、それも書く" :sample "At the top of Figure 4, the Input Layer accepts user messages through a thread-safe bounded queue, allowing follow-up messages to arrive while the agent is mid-execution.")
(defrule runtime-subsystems -> :instruction "ループの周りの部品の数と、各部品が別の関心を担うことを 1 文で書く" :sample "The periphery of Figure 4 shows seven subsystems, each addressing a distinct concern and detailed in a dedicated section.")
(defrule subsystem-list -> :instruction "周りの部品を、1 行に 1 つ部品の名前で挙げる" :frame "opendev.agent-core.subsystem.lisp")
(defrule runtime-modes -> :instruction "動作が複数のモードに分かれるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "The key architectural decision is that the system operates in two distinct modes, Plan Mode and Normal Mode, with the agent transitioning between them based on user commands or prompt triggers.")
(defrule runtime-routing -> :nucleus runtime-routing/check :condition runtime-routing/triggers)
(defrule runtime-routing/check -> :instruction "プロンプトが来たとき、どのモードで始めるかをどう決めるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "When a user prompt arrives, the MainAgent checks whether it should enter Plan Mode or proceed directly in Normal Mode.")
(defrule runtime-routing/triggers -> :instruction "計画モードに入る引き金を 1 文で書く" :sample "Two triggers activate Plan Mode: an explicit /plan command from the user, or a heuristic that detects planning intent in the prompt (e.g., requests to “design,” “architect,” or “plan” a change).")
(defrule runtime-delegated-planning -> :nucleus runtime-delegated-planning/delegate :elaboration-object-attribute runtime-delegated-planning/no-write)
(defrule runtime-delegated-planning/delegate -> :instruction "計画を専用の部下に任せる構えを 1 文で書く" :sample "Rather than switching the main agent into a restricted mode via dedicated plan-management tools, OpenDev delegates planning to a first-class Planner subagent.")
(defrule runtime-delegated-planning/no-write -> :instruction "計画の間に書き込みをどう封じるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Write operations are excluded from the subagent’s tool schema entirely: the LLM never sees tool definitions it cannot use, eliminating the possibility of write attempts during planning.")
(defrule runtime-planner-stages -> :nucleus runtime-planner-stages/stages :elaboration-process-step runtime-planner-stages/steps)
(defrule runtime-planner-stages/stages -> :instruction "計画役が行う段階の数を 1 文で書く" :sample "The Planner subagent executes in three stages visible in Figure 5.")
(defrule runtime-planner-stages/steps -> :instruction "段階を 1 項目ずつ、段階の名前と何を行うかで書く" :sample "First, it explores the codebase using read-only tools: reading files, searching code, listing directory contents, and resolving symbol definitions. / Second, it analyzes the findings, identifying patterns, evaluating risks, considering trade-offs, and determining the sequence of changes needed. / Third, it writes a structured plan to a file in the scratch directory, containing seven sections: goal, context, files to modify, new files to create, implementation steps, verification criteria, and risks." :kind bullet)
(defrule runtime-plan-review -> :instruction "計画を書き終えた後、何を誰に返し、利用者がどう選ぶかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Upon completion, the Planner returns the plan file path to the main agent.")
(defrule runtime-normal-mode -> :instruction "計画の外での、通常の動作を 1 文で書く" :sample "Normal Mode is the default and only operating state.")
(defrule runtime-replanning -> :instruction "実行中に予期しない結果に出会ったときの対処を 1 文で書く" :sample "During execution, if the agent encounters unexpected results (such as a test failure that reveals a deeper issue, a dependency conflict, or a scope change), it can spawn the Planner subagent again with the current codebase state as context, producing a revised plan that accounts for what has changed since the original plan was approved.")
(defrule runtime-plan-design-rationale -> :instruction "計画を部下に任せる設計の利点を 1 文で書く" :sample "This yields three advantages: (1) no state machine means no risk of getting stuck in plan mode; (2) the Planner can be spawned concurrently with other subagents (e.g., a Code Explorer for parallel analysis); and (3) the tool surface is reduced from four tools to one (present_plan), reducing cognitive load on the LLM.")
(defrule changes -> :instruction "計画の設計が経た転換を、1 行に 1 つ、置き換えた設計の名前で挙げる" :frame "opendev.design-change.lisp")
